(3203624, 446089, 48471, '<td valign="top">Compositionally, this photo is great, because the centered composition follows naturally. I don´t like that it isn´t monochrome, a simple play with light, instead having the colors of human skin opposing the white of the music sheet. A small detail, but not such a big deal would be asking your model to remove the ring. All these, small observations from the technical point.<br/> <br/>Regarding the story, this photo is confusing to me, because it´s periphery is so smooth and pleasant (lovely hands and music sheet), but then at the center is this big dark noisy O, punching my face. I don´t understand the title either: it might work as Jazz, or whatever, but this photo doesn´t say Round midnight to me, despite the association of the sax´s O with the clock.<br/> <br/>Still, a very good photo, which, if black and white, I could see hanging on the walls of some jazz bar.</td>', 'Compositionally, this photo is great, because the centered composition follows naturally. I don´t like that it isn´t monochrome, a simple play with light, instead having the colors of human skin opposing the white of the music sheet. A small detail, but not such a big deal would be asking your model to remove the ring. All these, small observations from the technical point. Regarding the story, this photo is confusing to me, because it´s periphery is so smooth and pleasant (lovely hands and music sheet), but then at the center is this big dark noisy O, punching my face. I don´t understand the title either: it might work as Jazz, or whatever, but this photo doesn´t say Round midnight to me, despite the association of the sax´s O with the clock. Still, a very good photo, which, if black and white, I could see hanging on the walls of some jazz bar.', '2007-01-10 01:42:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(3203630, 444890, 3724, '<td valign="top"><br/>voted 9... bos.  A remarkable portrait of Fouzia, a beautiful, peaceful expression. I wish him well - but also a brutal and startling confrontation to the reality and effect of disease.  <br/></td>', 'voted 9... bos.  A remarkable portrait of Fouzia, a beautiful, peaceful expression. I wish him well - but also a brutal and startling confrontation to the reality and effect of disease.  ', '2007-01-10 01:43:47.000000', NULL, 0),
