(3241567, 444451, 16197, '<td valign="top"><b>From the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>First Off I want to say WOW!, this is a great shot.  <br/> <br/><b>Colour</b>;<br/>As I look into this image, I light grays, darks grays and blues.  The blue is very well used, it is the strongest colour here and brings you right to the center.<br/>The grays I believe are very evenly balanced and creates a large amount of depth to the image.  Which to me is a good thing.<br/> <br/><b>DOF/Focus</b>;<br/>You have strong focus here on the center light.  It breaks away from the background without looking placed.  I really enjoy the narrow dof with this image. As you see the edge/corner it creates your environment and gives more connectivity to the image for the viewers.<br/> <br/><b>Post</b>;<br/>It seems you have a firm grasp of editing. No areas of the image are overly ''shopped'' and without knowing better, this image could pass for straight from the camera.<br/> <br/><b>Off Items</b>;<br/>For me personally, as I look at this image, I do have a strong since of center, however, the other blue lights make me feel like there is something on the corner of my eye.  For me they seem to be a slight distraction.  I understand it is a string of lights, and not really a shot you can set up,  But, you might play with angles to get a less obtrusive feeling.<br/> <br/>Also, the slush/ice in the lower left corner of the image is also a slight distraction.  If you were able maybe brushing it off or to the side would have evened that area more so.  Because it is on the back end of your narrow dof, it stands out a bit more.<br/> <br/><b>Other</b>;<br/>Being ''centered composition'' challenge, it makes me curious as to other compositions you may come up with.  This is a very dramatic find and excellently executed.<br/> <br/>Nice Job<br/> <br/>Andrew ''littlegett''</td>', 'From the Critique Club  First Off I want to say WOW!, this is a great shot.   Colour;As I look into this image, I light grays, darks grays and blues.  The blue is very well used, it is the strongest colour here and brings you right to the center.The grays I believe are very evenly balanced and creates a large amount of depth to the image.  Which to me is a good thing. DOF/Focus;You have strong focus here on the center light.  It breaks away from the background without looking placed.  I really enjoy the narrow dof with this image. As you see the edge/corner it creates your environment and gives more connectivity to the image for the viewers. Post;It seems you have a firm grasp of editing. No areas of the image are overly ''shopped'' and without knowing better, this image could pass for straight from the camera. Off Items;For me personally, as I look at this image, I do have a strong since of center, however, the other blue lights make me feel like there is something on the corner of my eye.  For me they seem to be a slight distraction.  I understand it is a string of lights, and not really a shot you can set up,  But, you might play with angles to get a less obtrusive feeling. Also, the slush/ice in the lower left corner of the image is also a slight distraction.  If you were able maybe brushing it off or to the side would have evened that area more so.  Because it is on the back end of your narrow dof, it stands out a bit more. Other;Being ''centered composition'' challenge, it makes me curious as to other compositions you may come up with.  This is a very dramatic find and excellently executed. Nice Job Andrew ''littlegett''', '2007-01-16 18:04:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(3242030, 446104, 48228, '<td valign="top">Perfect in this format, re the square crop..... <br/> <br/>One usually see these type of images in a landscape format, but I love it like this, as it gives this image the perfect "WOW" factor.....</td>', 'Perfect in this format, re the square crop.....  One usually see these type of images in a landscape format, but I love it like this, as it gives this image the perfect "WOW" factor.....', '2007-01-16 19:24:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(3243235, 444651, 62318, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Initial Impression - Great exposure and contrast but ultimately lacking in subject interest.<br/> <br/>Composition - Overall the composition is okay. I get what you were going for, isolating the sign agaist the white wall background. You are right to go with a centered composition here. However, I think the angle of the sign is a real deterent, but that probably has more to do with the wall as the background...<br/> <br/>Technicals - The exposure is actually pretty good. Sharpness is good. There is a tilt, but it works for this image. Techniquely I think the image is strong.<br/> <br/>Possible Suggestions: <br/>You might try a higher plane, rather than looking up it might be beneficial to look straight on. Normally I don''t like vignetting, but in this case accentuating the sign by a strong vignette I think would help. Along the same plan allowing to see more of the bricks in the background "may" also help with a stronger composition. Maybe bring out the white a little more, especially in the "Stop" in the sign. Normally, I am not a strong component of post, but I think a little added dramatic style done in post would have really worked well.</td>', '*Critique Club* Initial Impression - Great exposure and contrast but ultimately lacking in subject interest. Composition - Overall the composition is okay. I get what you were going for, isolating the sign agaist the white wall background. You are right to go with a centered composition here. However, I think the angle of the sign is a real deterent, but that probably has more to do with the wall as the background... Technicals - The exposure is actually pretty good. Sharpness is good. There is a tilt, but it works for this image. Techniquely I think the image is strong. Possible Suggestions: You might try a higher plane, rather than looking up it might be beneficial to look straight on. Normally I don''t like vignetting, but in this case accentuating the sign by a strong vignette I think would help. Along the same plan allowing to see more of the bricks in the background "may" also help with a stronger composition. Maybe bring out the white a little more, especially in the "Stop" in the sign. Normally, I am not a strong component of post, but I think a little added dramatic style done in post would have really worked well.', '2007-01-16 23:15:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(3244037, 446631, 31133, '<td valign="top">Skip, this is lovely! I''ve noticed this beautiful lighthouse shot when browsing, but didn''t notice that it was you who entered it. This is your first entry since Scratchin and Pickin, and I''m so happy to see you back in the challenges, or at least one &lt;--- enough to give me hope that you might be back in the challenges :-) The stars are so beautiful. In your notes, you write about it being too late to catch the lighthouse rays - boy, that would''ve been something wonderful if you could''ve, but this is just great as it is. You''re an inspiration.</td>', 'Skip, this is lovely! I''ve noticed this beautiful lighthouse shot when browsing, but didn''t notice that it was you who entered it. This is your first entry since Scratchin and Pickin, and I''m so happy to see you back in the challenges, or at least one <--- enough to give me hope that you might be back in the challenges :-) The stars are so beautiful. In your notes, you write about it being too late to catch the lighthouse rays - boy, that would''ve been something wonderful if you could''ve, but this is just great as it is. You''re an inspiration.', '2007-01-17 01:26:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(3250281, 444892, 51112, '<td valign="top">Well this kinda got smashed during the challenge. I have to say it does not have the crispness and color vibrance of other pics in the challenge...<br/>The lack of contrast is intended, it shows how the leaf blends into the background as it fades away.<br/>For the few who love it, I really love the way this picture turned out as well :-)</td>', 'Well this kinda got smashed during the challenge. I have to say it does not have the crispness and color vibrance of other pics in the challenge...The lack of contrast is intended, it shows how the leaf blends into the background as it fades away.For the few who love it, I really love the way this picture turned out as well :-)', '2007-01-18 03:55:28.000000', NULL, 0),
